MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Blade Runner 2049 felt worth trying because my interest in Star Trek gives me a reason to explore another science fiction story.",
    "That connection was enough to make me curious, although it does not mean I would enjoy every science fiction film."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Sully and Agatha Christie's Ordeal By Innocence did not connect clearly to the science fiction interest guiding my choice right now.",
    "The Shape of Water's fantasy romance premise did not offer the same appeal as science fiction, and I could not assess the unidentified items from the information available."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The selection felt too broad if my interest in one television series was taken to mean I wanted films and television stories of any kind.",
    "Treating fantasy and science fiction as interchangeable would miss why Blade Runner 2049 appealed to me more than The Shape of Water."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My identifiable Star Trek interaction provides a specific reason to suggest science fiction, though most of my history gives too little information to establish broader tastes.",
    "I choose selectively: I need a recognizable story or premise that connects to my interests before I am willing to try something."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "Blade Runner 2049 connected plausibly to my Star Trek interest, while the other identifiable suggestions stretched beyond what I wanted this time."
}
